# 103 - Configuration Documentation

**Phase:** 1 (Foundation)
**Effect:** Developers can understand and modify server settings
**Status:** Completed (2026-01-29)

---

## The Effect

When a developer opens this project, they can quickly understand:
- What settings have been changed from defaults
- Why those changes were made
- How to adjust settings for their needs

This removes the barrier of "read the source" or "guess and test" when configuring the server.

---

## What This Solved

### Before
- 50+ modified settings in worldserver.conf with no explanation
- Custom paths scattered across authserver and worldserver configs
- Module configurations undocumented
- Lua script timings hardcoded with no reference

Developers had to:
1. Read raw .conf files (500+ lines each)
2. Consult external AzerothCore wiki
3. Diff against default configs to find changes
4. Guess at the purpose of custom values

### After
One document (`docs/configuration.md`) that lists:
- All modified settings grouped by category
- The purpose of each modification
- Quick reference for file locations
- Lua script timing constants

---

## What Was Created

### docs/configuration.md

Comprehensive reference organized by domain:

**Path Configuration**
- Custom MySQL port (3307)
- Project-local data directory
- Lua script paths

**Game Balance** (50+ settings)
- Movement: Slower walk/run speeds, increased fall damage
- Progression: 3x talent points every 1/3 level, 10x rest XP
- Economy: Vendor prices scaled, 25x repair costs
- Death: No resurrection sickness, instant corpse reclaim
- Creatures: No leash, extended assist radius
- Visibility: Extended view distance, disabled node sparkles
- Instances: Enter at any level, solo raids enabled
- Cross-Faction: All interactions enabled

**Module Configuration**
- ALE (Eluna) script loading
- Playerbots settings

**Lua Script Constants**
- Ambush spawn interval (40s base, random walk)
- Traveler spawn interval (130s)
- Treasure spawn interval (100s)
- Spawn distances (ambush 120-160 yards, travelers 50-100 yards)

